WEBVTT

00:00:05.844 --> 00:00:14.537
A 58 millimeter receipt can hold a long basket, but the printer output has different limits from a PDF page. We will inspect both before printing.

00:00:22.163 --> 00:00:29.389
Open the Receipt 58 mm example. It uses a continuous roll profile and fictional supermarket sale data.

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:46.058
Edit the sale with a realistic grocery basket. The line items and totals now come from the same sample data.

00:00:50.765 --> 00:00:59.343
Choose Roll to inspect the complete receipt as one strip. The roll ends with a single cut; the PDF page height does not limit the ESC/POS roll.

00:01:01.703 --> 00:01:11.216
Open the Print settings and check the 58 millimeter width, 203 dpi and printable printer columns. The line and cut counts summarize the generated output.

00:01:17.885 --> 00:01:28.657
Preview PDF to check its paper layout, then open ESC/POS to inspect the actual decoded printer text and warnings. Unsupported styling may be simplified for a thermal printer.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:43.113
Download the .bin file to send the generated bytes to a compatible receipt printer. Check paper feed, character set and cutting on the target device first.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:54.392
The same report can offer a paged PDF for email and a continuous roll for checkout, but always verify the physical printer result.

00:01:56.196 --> 00:01:57.121
